## Change

- `RequestSendFailureCause(pub String)` and
  `TransactionCallbackError(pub String)` exposed writable public tuple fields
  with no Java public-field counterpart.
- Both wrappers now store their strings privately and expose public `new` and
  read-only `message()` methods. Core/Producer call sites use these methods.
- Compile-fail Rustdoc examples verify external callers cannot access field
  `0`. The compatibility map now connects the accessors to Java throwable
  message construction and `getMessage()` behavior.

